 ## Overview
-Hierarchical Vector Quantization (HVQ) is a lossy compression algorithm for volumetric data that achieves high compression ratios (typically 20:1) with minimal artifacts, specifically designed to allow GPU-based decompression and rendering [S2, S3, unofficial]. Unlike wavelet-based methods that require serial CPU decompression before transfer, HVQ encodes data into an RGB index texture, enabling parallel, on-the-fly decoding directly on the graphics chip to minimize CPU-to-GPU data transfer [S2, S3, unofficial].
