 5.  **File Format (`.l3vq`):** The binary file structure is: 1. Flag (8-bit): Endianness indicator [S2, unofficial]. 2. Integer size (bytes): Machine-independent integer size [S2, unofficial]. 3. Mode (variable): 1 if compressed from difference of two time steps, 0 if original data [S2, unofficial]. 4. Dimensions: `sizeX`, `sizeY`, `sizeZ` storing $D_x'/4 \times D_y'/4 \times D_z'/4$ respectively [S2, unofficial]. 5. `scaleDiff0`: Largest absolute value in `Difference Level 0` [S2, unofficial]. 6. `scaleDetl0`: Largest absolute value in `Detail Level 0` [S2, unofficial]. 7. Codebook A: 256 $\times$ 64 bytes [S2, unofficial]. 8. Codebook B: 256 $\times$ 8 bytes [S2, unofficial]. 9. RGB Triplets: $D_x'/4 \times D_y'/4 \times D_z'/4$ triplets [S2, unofficial].
