 ## Background
-Hierarchical Vector Quantization was proposed by Jens Schneider and Rüdiger Westermann at the Technical University Munich [S3, unofficial]. It was published in 2003 as part of the work on "Compression Domain Volume Rendering" [S3, unofficial]. The method builds on vector quantization theory and aims to address the limitation of limited texture memory in graphics hardware by allowing direct decoding and rendering on the GPU [S3, unofficial]. It is comparable to wavelet-based compression in fidelity but offers the advantage of parallel GPU decompression [S2, unofficial].
